{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#picture.3", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.1", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.4", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.6", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.7", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl/type:sasl-init/field:mechanism.2", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl/type:sasl-outcome.1", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#picture.6"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "PLAIN on the client's side: the server announces one mechanism, the init names it and carries the mechanism's own credential block as the initial response \u2014 which this layer passes through as the binary field the artifact declares it as \u2014 the outcome establishes the layer, and the peers exchange protocol headers again for AMQP and then open. ANONYMOUS is the model; PLAIN differs only in that the initial response is not empty.", "start": "connection:START", "steps": [{"bytes": "414d515003010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515003010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001802010000005340c00b01c00801a305504c41494e", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}, "note": "the server's announcement, in its own frame: the dialogue's state is the layer's, not the table's, so the connection state does not move"}, {"bytes": "0000002602010000005341c01902a305504c41494ea00f006175746863696400706173737764", "direction": "send", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}, "note": "the initial response is RFC4616's authzid NUL authcid NUL passwd, which the artifact declares as opaque binary and this layer therefore does not read"}, {"bytes": "0000001002010000005344c003015000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:START", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000000005310c00901a106636c69656e74", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPEN_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000000005310c00901a106736572766572", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPENED", "status": "admitted"}}], "vector": "sasl-plain-client-init-to-open"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#picture.3", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.1", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.4", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.6", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.7", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl/type:sasl-mechanisms/field:sasl-server-mechanisms.1", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl/type:sasl-outcome.1", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#picture.6"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "the server's side of the same exchange, and the other end of the negotiation: it announces two mechanisms and it is the partner that chooses, so the two vectors together pin the membership rule from both sides rather than from one end only.", "start": "connection:START", "steps": [{"bytes": "414d515003010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_RCVD", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515003010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000002302010000005340c01601c01302a305504c41494ea309414e4f4e594d4f5553", "direction": "send", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000002602010000005341c01902a305504c41494ea00f006175746863696400706173737764", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}, "note": "the partner chose the stronger of the two, which is the freedom this layer does not decide: see the contract's record of `mechanism.2`"}, {"bytes": "0000001002010000005344c003015000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:START", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_RCVD", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000000005310c00901a106636c69656e74", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPEN_RCVD", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000000005310c00901a106736572766572", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPENED", "status": "admitted"}}], "vector": "sasl-plain-server"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#picture.3", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.1", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.4", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.6", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.7", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl/type:sasl-outcome.1", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#picture.6"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "EXTERNAL with the challenge-and-response step happening twice, which is what picture.6's footnote allows \u2014 it 'can occur zero or more times depending on the details of the SASL mechanism chosen'. The mechanism's own data is opaque to this layer, so what the vector pins is the shape: each round's challenge is the server's and each response the client's, and the dialogue still ends at the outcome. Compare `sasl-plain-client-init-to-open`, where the step occurs zero times.", "start": "connection:START", "steps": [{"bytes": "414d515003010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515003010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001b02010000005340c00e01c00b01a30845585445524e414c", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000002c02010000005341c01f02a30845585445524e414ca012636c69656e74406578616d706c652e6f7267", "direction": "send", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}, "note": "EXTERNAL's initial response is the authorization identity the peer asks the server to use \u2014 opaque binary here, as every mechanism's data is"}, {"bytes": "0000001702010000005342c00a01a0076e6f6e63652d31", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001702010000005343c00a01a0077265706c792d31", "direction": "send", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001702010000005342c00a01a0076e6f6e63652d32", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001702010000005343c00a01a0077265706c792d32", "direction": "send", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001002010000005344c003015000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:START", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000000005310c00901a106636c69656e74", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPEN_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000000005310c00901a106736572766572", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPENED", "status": "admitted"}}], "vector": "sasl-external-client-two-rounds"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#picture.3", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.1", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.4", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.6", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.7", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl/type:sasl-init/field:mechanism.2", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl/type:sasl-mechanisms/field:sasl-server-mechanisms.1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "what the negotiation actually constrains, and what it does not: the list carries three mechanisms, the init names the last of them, and the dialogue proceeds \u2014 the rule this layer enforces is *membership*, because that is the rule the artifact states ('If the selected mechanism is not supported by the receiving peer, it MUST close'). The artifact also says the list is ordered in decreasing preference and that a peer MUST authenticate using the highest-level profile it can handle; no security profile is defined anywhere in the pinned bytes, so that obligation is recorded in `Contracts/Sasl.lean` as unmodelled rather than enforced by a table this repository would have had to invent.", "start": "connection:START", "steps": [{"bytes": "414d515003010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515003010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000002d02010000005340c02001c01d03a305504c41494ea30845585445524e414ca309414e4f4e594d4f5553", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001902010000005341c00c01a309414e4f4e594d4f5553", "direction": "send", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001002010000005344c003015000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:START", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000000005310c00901a106636c69656e74", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPEN_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000000005310c00901a106736572766572", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPENED", "status": "admitted"}}], "vector": "sasl-mechanism-chosen-from-a-list"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#picture.3", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.1", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl.4", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl/type:sasl-outcome.1", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl/type:sasl-outcome/field:additional-data.u1", "amqp-core-security-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:security/section:sasl/type:sasl-code/choice:ok.u1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "the complement of `sasl-outcome-additional-data-on-failure`, and the reason that vector is about the field's *rule* rather than about the field: the artifact forbids additional-data on an unsuccessful outcome and allows it on a successful one, so an exclusion alone would be as wrong as the admission was. The layer establishes and the extra data is carried past it, uninterpreted.", "start": "connection:START", "steps": [{"bytes": "414d515003010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515003010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001c02010000005340c00f01c00c01a309414e4f4e594d4f5553", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001902010000005341c00c01a309414e4f4e594d4f5553", "direction": "send", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001002010000005344c003015000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:START", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:HDR_EXCH", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000000005310c00901a106636c69656e74", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPEN_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000000005310c00901a106736572766572", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "connection:OPENED", "status": "admitted"}}], "vector": "sasl-outcome-additional-data-on-success"}
